@startuml
title WIM – Diagramme de composants / déploiement

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #ffffff
  BorderColor #555555
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #ffffff
  BorderColor #555555
}

actor "Navigateur\n(PWA installable)" as Browser

node "Render – Site statique\nwim-web.onrender.com" as WebHost {
  component "apps/web\n(Vite + React 19)" as Web
  component "Service Worker\n(sw.js)" as SW
}

node "Render – Service Node\nwimapi.onrender.com" as ApiHost {
  component "apps/api\n(Express + Prisma)" as Api
  component "Workers BullMQ\n(in-process)" as Workers
}

database "PostgreSQL\n(Render)" as PG
database "Redis\n(denylist + BullMQ)" as Redis

cloud "Stripe" as Stripe
cloud "Resend\n(e-mail)" as Resend
cloud "Web Push\n(VAPID)" as Push

Browser --> Web : HTTPS
Web ..> SW : enregistre (prod)
Web --> Api : fetch(credentials: include)\ncookie httpOnly wim_token + CSRF (Origin/Referer)

Api --> PG : Prisma (SQL)
Api --> Redis : jti denylist + tokenVersion
Workers --> Redis : files wim-alerts / wim-maintenance
Workers --> PG : lecture/écriture (rappels, purge, digest)

Api --> Stripe : Checkout / Portal / sync
Stripe --> Api : Webhook (raw body, signature HMAC)
Workers --> Resend : rappels + digest (best-effort)
Workers --> Push : notifications push

note bottom
Frontière de sécurité : le cookie wim_token est httpOnly + SameSite=none
en prod (sous-domaines Render différents) ; les mutations exigent un
Origin/Referer autorisé (csrfGuard). Le webhook Stripe est monté AVANT
express.json() et s'authentifie par signature, hors du chemin cookie/CSRF.
Les workers tournent dans le même processus que l'API.
end note
@enduml
